CHAPTER VI
INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS
Article 11
(1) In the case of providing protection to women and children victims of violence, the regional government may establish an Integrated Service Center (PPT).
jdih.pakpakbharatkab.go.id - 8 - (2) The establishment and development of PPT shall be adjusted to the development of priority needs, regional financial capacity, and institutional capacity of existing personnel in the region.
(3) PPT as referred to in paragraph (1) may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as P2TP2A, Safe Houses, Child Social Protection Houses, Trauma Center Houses, Women's Social Protection Houses, Shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
(4) Forms of services implemented by PPT include:
a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal assistance;
e. repatriation;
f. social reintegration.
(5) In providing protection to women and children victims of violence, PPT is obligated to:
a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to victims; b. organize protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims; d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperate with witness and victim protection institutions, social protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community or other institutions for victims' health recovery;
e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for victims; f. maintain confidentiality of victims;
g. provide fulfillment of legal assistance for victims;
h. in the case that integrated service provision is carried out through networking, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services needed by victims.
(6) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

CHAPTER V
PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 9
(1) To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the regional government shall conduct empowerment and awareness-raising to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government shall undertake efforts as follows:
a. improvement of the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening of accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. opening of employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern towards prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and
g. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

